-   "state_note": "[2026-09-19] #542 queued after #541 (it also corrects #541's #194 comment); drafts in _scratchpad/waifk/.  FOUND 2026-09-18 by GXEMUL (2) [e8a2bc] while filling the alphavmkill brief, WITNESSED at rung 3 the same evening on the committed binary (no build).  DYNTRANS_PC_TO_POINTERS_GENERIC assumes a failed fetch translation raised an exception and moved the PC; it retries at cpu->pc and, on a second failure, fatal()s and exit(1)s.  alpha_translate_v2p fails WITHOUT moving the PC, so the retry is the same miss.  RESEARCH: codex_research_jA_20260918.txt (a bare `running = 0' falls through with no paddr; a bare `return' leaves next_ic unset).  PASS 1 (panel_20260919_003152, ten answers + fable5 LAST): option (e), GENERIC, THREE hunks -- stop the CPU with next_ic = &nothing_call (no +1), an entry guard in run_instr, and an epilogue guard keyed on the sentinel (NEVER on !running).  The round is next after #541.",
+   "state_note": "[2026-09-21 16:2x] #542 IN WORK (e8a2bc).  KILL TABLE 2 = 24 of 24 AS PREDICTED on the 43-row v3.1 instrument (killtable2_20260921/), clone restored cmp-clean with the sentinel removed, and the five mutants pass 2's findings bought each die on exactly the row that finding added.  M6 reds `stop msg2' and `miss count2', which were GREEN under it in table 1 -- the pre-table CHANNEL repair measured, not asserted.  PASS 3 (panel_20260921_152240): 6 answered, the kimi CLI WALLED mid-answer (190 KB at 100% novel) and codex REFUSED mid-answer (65 KB at 81% novel) -- both recorded as seat failures with their bodies read.  NO seat challenged the C; one SHIP and five SHIP-WITH-CHANGES, every change to the record.  *** AND A FLOOR BREACH: *** the Opus 5 seat (verified CLEAN claude-opus-5 -- the first non-fallback Opus answer in days, on a neutrally-worded brief) found S6 computing a CTRL-T that no row read, and grok built the mutant that lives in the hole -- an entry guard whose PC advance is conditioned on NOT single-stepping passes all 43 rows, because S3 is stepped and S6 scored no PC.  L2, repaired in-round: v3.2 adds `pc6' (44 rows), consuming a value the probe already computed.  OWED: table 3 on v3.2, then pass 4.  Records corrected from pass 3: the property claim is re-scoped to its ALPHA witness (the hunks compile everywhere and are witnessed nowhere else), and the disclosure `every path that installs the sentinel has cleared running' is FALSE -- the breakpoint goto at cpu_dyntrans.c:1848 jumps past `running = 0' at :2014.",
