regress/artifacts/fableheldform\design_20261018\codex_fhfp1.err:902:tools\pipeline\matrix.html:4662:  -- against the wired controls in the same batch: sh_iprbcd_probe.py, sgi_re_rgb_probe.py, gdrom_default_probe.py and diff_wdc_identify.c all ARE referenced.  `run.sh` runs an explicit `GATES=(...)` list and the four appear nowhere outside `regress/` and the wiring checker itself. *** TWO OF THE FOUR ARE HIGH-SEVERITY ROWS.  Delete `| (vaddr &amp; ((1ULL &lt;&lt; pageSizeShift) - 1))` from `memory_alpha.c` and a HIGH page-walk defect is back with a CLEAN BATTERY. *** **THE SEAT EXPLICITLY DECLINED TO CLAIM THIS AS NEW, which is the right call and is why it lands here rather than as a fresh row:** `check_probe_wiring.py` already classifies all four as `CLASS_WITNESS` -- correctly, by the ladder&#x27;s witness/detector timing line -- and its own entry for `lca_confbus_probe.py` says *&quot;but this probe RUNS IN NO GATE, so the coverage exists and is never executed: wiringcliff&quot;*. *** BUT THAT CHECKER IS UNCOMMITTED, so **nothing in any committed tree reports this today.** ***  The four closures are HONEST -- their `witness:` says `probe:`, which is exactly what it is -- and what is absent is STANDING DEFENCE.  The seat&#x27;s disposition, adopted: this belongs in each round record as a DISCLOSED RESIDUAL on those four rows, not only as one filed id, because a reader of `alphapfnoffset` alone cannot see it.  *** SCOPE NOTE FROM THE FABLE ADJUDICATION, 2026-09-17: MAKE SURE THE FOUR `CLASS_WITNESS` PROBES ARE IN THIS ROW&#x27;S SCOPE, NOT ONLY THE DATED EXEMPTIONS. ***  This row&#x27;s own title is about the EXEMPT table expiring, and the four unwired witnesses (`lca_confbus_probe.py`, `lca_confwidth_probe.py`, `alpha_pfnoffset_probe.py`, `alpha_harness_probe.py`) are a different population -- classified `CLASS_WITNESS`, never exempted, simply never run. *** AND A TRAP THAT WOULD BITE THE FIX: `lca_confwidth_probe.py` MUST NOT BE WIRED AS-IS. ***  It scores **2/6 at HEAD** (measured 2026-09-17, `regress/artifacts/lcaconfwidth/head_20260917/`) because `#518` replaced the IOC_CONF kill with a decline.  Wiring it produces a PHANTOM RED; the remedy there is RE-PIN OR RETIRE, under the oracle-correction rule&#x27;s order -- re-pin first, measure the committed build red under the new expectations, then change anything. **AND THE COMMITTED TREE ALREADY KNOWS**, which sharpens the gap rather than excusing it: `check_probe_wiring.py` carries all four as `CLASS_WITNESS` with their scores.  *The gap is the FAILING, not the knowing* -- the checker deliberately does not fail on that class.  *** OWNER DECISION 2026-09-17: STAGGER -- wire the cheap ones, re-date the rest with SEPARATED deadlines and the owing round named on each.  A blanket extension was declined for the reason this checker&#x27;s own header gives: debt that expires, not debt that disappears -- and the present cliff exists because ONE deliberate alignment of two #442 debts was then copied by nine later exemptions. ***  THE ELEVEN ARE NOT ONE JOB.  Derived 2026-09-17 by reading each probe rather than its exemption text, and they fall into FIVE classes: (1) THREE ALPHA PROBES -- alpha_tbi, lca_badval, lca_isalane -- share ONE blocker; (2) FOUR wdc_* probes are TWO-LEG DIFFERENTIALS needing a single-leg mode, and two of those additionally need rig images the battery does not build; (3) fbpending_drain is REPORT-ONLY until EXPECT_CAP is designed; (4) mk48_nvram needs an mvme187 leg on gate_m88k_rounding.sh; (5) ppc_rldicl lacks the RESULT/CONTROL protocol AND is on the do-not-commit list, so it CANNOT be wired at all and must be re-dated whatever else happens.  *** THE FINDING THAT CHANGES THE PLAN, AND IT IS A WRONG PREMISE IN THE EXEMPTION&#x27;S OWN REASON.  Measured, not reasoned. ***  All three Alpha entries read &#x27;no gate runs an Alpha machine; gate_crossfamily.sh is the named home and giving it one is a harness round&#x27;.  That premise is TRUE OF RIGS AND FALSE OF PROBES.  gate_crossfamily.sh (gate 5) drives BOOTABLE RIG IMAGES through drive_guest.py, so &#x27;an Alpha leg&#x27; reads as &#x27;obtain a bootable Alpha guest&#x27;, which genuinely is a harness round.  But measured against the probes themselves: NONE of the three references a disk image at all; each execs `-E alpha&#x27; as a rung-3 COLD-DEBUGGER probe; and each already emits the parseable token a gate scores (ALPHATBI_RESULT, LCABADVAL_RESULT, LCAISALANE_RESULT).  gate_arm.sh already wires probes in exactly this shape -- `python3 &lt;probe&gt;.py &quot;$BIN&quot; &gt; &quot;$LOG&quot; 2&gt;&amp;1 || true&#x27; followed by count rows -- and runs SIX of them.  So what these three need is a PROBE SECTION, not an Alpha rig: roughly six lines apiece in an idiom the tree already uses six times.  ONE gate run discharges all three.  THE STAGGER, therefore: WIRE the three Alpha probes into gate 5 as a probe section (they also fit its stated purpose -- &#x27;non-MIPS CPU cores actually execute guest code&#x27; -- since a cold-debugger probe executing real Alpha instructions is precisely that).  RE-DATE the other eight to separated deadlines by CLASS, so the next cliff cannot re-form: the four wdc_* together behind the single-leg-mode instrument change, fbpending_drain behind EXPECT_CAP, mk48_nvram behind the mvme187 leg, ppc_rldicl on its own and longest, since it is blocked by a do-not-commit constraint rather than by work.  NOT DONE IN THIS TURN, DELIBERATELY: the exemption block states that each wiring owes ONE CLEAN GATE RUN proving it green before it ships, citing FOUR probes that shipped latently RED because the commit adding them never fired the gate.  A gate run contends with the #531 measurement in flight, so the wiring lands with its gate run and not before.  The deletion rule is already recorded here and is followed: a wired probe that KEEPS its exemption is a STALE EXEMPTION and this checker reds on it, so each entry is DELETED in the SAME edit that adds its wiring.</span></span><span class="state st-in work">in work</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-in work"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">2026-09-09</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;2026-09-09&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-09 — RULING-REV2 — SECOND REVISION, on 7 of 9 seats (opus5 now landed; agy not fired).  THE FIRST REVISION, ONE ENTRY ABOVE, IS SUPERSEDED IN THREE PLACES AND SAYS SO HERE RATHER THAN BEING EDITED: it kept fbpending design-blocked on a cap derivation (the cap is the WRONG INSTRUMENT -- the bound is already gated by an equality); it kept four WDC files in one round (they are 3 + 1, and _sig&#x27;s media blocker is MEASURED FALSE); and it counted six obligations (there are SEVEN, and my own deriver printed the seventh at check_probe_wiring.py:1328 and I read past it -- the third correlate-not-the-property error of the day, all mine).  Every Opus claim relied on here was re-verified in the tree before this was written: gate_offline.sh:1084/:1165, check_probe_wiring.py:1328, sig_probe.py:75, gate_asan_sweep.sh:99.  DISPOSITION, REV 2.  (1) TWO rounds, not one: `wdcaltoffleg&#x27; owns the three altoffset files (one module, one rig, one media family; the parent&#x27;s `ok&#x27; first; _4bit&#x27;s single-leg form is an ORACLE CHOICE and says so; _sig owes an oracle REDESIGN, not a bolted-on contract); `wdcsingleleg&#x27; is RETITLED to addtoinbuf alone, with the poisoned image and the endianness axis as its dependencies.  (2) THREE things are decidable TODAY and all three go in the wiringcliff commit after #516: hpcmips WIRED into gate_asan_sweep.sh BEFORE the :99 gate_skip, additive rows named, its EXEMPT entry DELETED in the same edit; fbpending WIRED with NO CAP as an apparatus-rot row named for what it tests, its EXEMPT entry deleted in the same edit, and the SM_EXEMPT fbpendin