.out, probe47r.py) and the loop row (fix 48/48, M_msr_argmask 47/48, HEAD 18/48; probe48.py).  Owed together: one repair, a FULL re-table on the 48-row probe, and its own pass.  Dissent carried: deepseek, glm and kimi-k3 graded M_msr_argmask OWED; grok, codex, minimax, agy and the Opus seat graded it disclosure.  OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md carries the full entry.  Also the gate 14 parser: a dead vehicle (CONTROL=DEAD, no REDS line) is reported as malformed, and a log with one row replaced by a duplicate of another passes -- no check establishes row IDENTITY or uniqueness (the Opus seat; GPT-6 Astra&#x27;s confirmation).  ||  [2026-10-09, Fable 5.1&#x27;s #562 adjudication] ITEM: gate_arm.sh&#x27;s `arm_msrmode rows failed` check (grep -E &#x27; want=&#x27; | grep -cE &#x27; FAIL &#x27;) is green only because the probe truncates notes to 64 characters, which cuts the `kill 14` note before its &#x27; FAIL &#x27; text; a future note edit can turn the gate RED falsely -- loud, the safe direction.  Key the check on the row&#x27;s verdict column, not on free text.  ||  [2026-10-09, Fable 5.1&#x27;s regress review of #562 (regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/regress_20261009/fable5_regress562.md), notes]: `tbit` and `encl2` have no diag line -- a diag_unimpl call on each is a cheap addition for THIS repair (an AST change, so not #562&#x27;s); and `rows failed` is green only because note[:64] cuts kill 14&#x27;s note before its &#x27; FAIL &#x27; text, already filed here as the gate-parser bullet.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">headerstaleobj</span><span class="ttl">build trees: a HEADER change leaves stale objects -- the build tracks no header dependencies, propagate_all_trees.sh removes only ${F%.c}.o, and the two-part clearance ([ binary -nt source ]) cannot see an object compiled against the old header</span><span class="tip">build trees: a HEADER change leaves stale objects -- the build tracks no header dependencies, propagate_all_trees.sh removes only ${F%.c}.o, and the two-part clearance ([ binary -nt source ]) cannot see an object compiled against the old header — witness: harness:#562&#x27;s gate 14 run -- regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/gate14_20261009/gate14_run1.out (xscale ANCHOR_ISRC/ANCHOR_EXC red, 28/30) and gate14_20261009/xscale_ab.out: a HEAD build 30/30 twice, both incrementally rebuilt #562 builds 28/30 twice — note: FOUND 2026-10-09 by #562&#x27;s gate 14.  #562 inserted `uint32_t mode_warned` into struct arm_cpu (src/include/cpu_arm.h) BEFORE i80321_inten/isrc, tmr0, tmr0_irq/tmr1_irq and tisr; dev_i80321.c is the only object outside src/cpus that touches them.  Every build that rebuilt only src/cpus/*.o (the carrier&#x27;s recipe, my propagate562.sh and every kill-table clone) linked a dev_i80321.o compiled against the OLD layout, so the device set isrc at the old offset and the guest read 0 -- gate 14&#x27;s xscale anchor red on the fix and green on HEAD, deterministically.  The two-part clearance PASSED on all three trees: the binary was newer than every source.  propagate_all_trees.sh can relink and report clearance success while header-dependent objects stay stale: `rm -f ${F%.c}.o` deletes nothing for a .h and the link recipe relinks unconditionally (GPT-6 Astra&#x27;s confirmation; this note first said the tool would report the header stale -- false).  SCOPE MEASURED: only dev_i80321.c reads a field after the insertion point; cd is the last member of struct cpu, so no subsequent struct cpu member shifted, and every other non-CPU ARM access precedes the insertion; the msrmode probe drives -E testarm, which attaches no i80321, so #562&#x27;s kill-table results are unaffected.  OWED: when a propagated path is a header, delete every object (or every object that includes it) and rebuild; and a third clearance part -- no object older than any edited header -- in the tool and the checkpoint step.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-in work"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">wdc473floor</span><span class="ttl">regress/diff_wdc_identify.c: #473&#x27;s re-arm/arm clamp detector passes all 128 rows under EIGHT one-token variants (bound moves at both clamps; first-byte-only content checks), and #495&#x27;s write guard is ungated</span><span class="tip">regress/diff_wdc_identify.c: #473&#x27;s re-arm/arm clamp detector passes all 128 rows under EIGHT one-token variants (bound moves at both clamps; first-byte-only content checks), and #495&#x27;s write guard is ungated — note: filed 2026-10-09 from the late REVIEW seats on wdcrearmzero (Fable 5.1 and Opus 5.5, both MEASURED in scratch clones; regress/artifacts/wdcrearmzero/review_20261009/).  Fable: the re-arm bound relaxed to 65536 or lowered to 16384, the arm bound relaxed to 65536, the re-arm operand swapped to atapi_received -- 0 of 128 red each; rows at 32767 and 32769 on each clamp kill all four (a just-PAST row alone cannot see a LOWERED bound).  Opus: Md_frozenj (codex&#x27;s, named on #473&#x27;s pass 2, never built), Md_revwalk (glm&#x27;s), Md_halfj, Md_armfrozen -- every content check reads only the chunk&#x27;s first byte; three rows kill all four and also HEAD with #495&#x27;s write guard removed.  Clause-(d) floor breach of shipped material: L2, a FOLLOW-UP round under the late-dissent rule (disposition 2), never under #473&#x27;s number.  OWNER 2026-10-09: this round FIRST, then the asiceventaddr closure, then armmmuvehicle.</span></span><span class="state st-in work">in work</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-in work"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-in work"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-in work"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-in work"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">armvecrecurse</span><span class="ttl">ARM MMU: an abort taken while the active page table does not map the vector page recurses through nested prefetch aborts until the HOST process dies (SIGSEGV after ~47,591 nested faults in 10.6 s)</span><span class="tip">ARM MMU: an abort taken while the active page table does not map the vector page recurses through nested prefetch aborts until the HOST process dies (SIGSEGV after ~47,591 nested faults in 10.6 s) — note: filed 2026-10-09 from the Opus 5.5 seat&#x27;s armmmuvehicle pass-1 answer (MEASURED, regress/artifacts/armmmuvehicle/pass1_20261009/opus5/opus5_meas/meas3_base.out -- the run log, its status from waitpid -- and T3_vec_unmapped.txt, meas3.py&#x27;s head-and-tail excerpt of that transcript): unmodified -E testarm, the MMU on, section 0 through a coarse table whose page 0 is unmapped, one data abort -&gt; 47,591 nested &#x27;{ arm memory fault ...}&#x27; lines and &#x27;Exception caused no mode change?&#x27; warnings in 10.6 s (10,473,809 bytes), the process ended by signal 11; the &#x27;could not find physical address of the exception handler&#x27; exit in cpu_dyntrans.c appears ZERO times.  READ mechanism (Opus): arm_exception -&gt; quick_pc_to_pointers -&gt; the generic lookup -&gt; translate_v2p fails -&gt; arm_exception(PREF_ABT) -&gt; quick_pc_to_pointers -&gt; ... before control returns to the generic function&#x27;s second lookup.  A guest that unmaps its own vectors and takes any abort ends the host process: guest-drivable process death. The unlatched fault/warning diagnostics are also a flood (floodclass).  Vehicle: armmmuvehicle.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">sysasicbitmask31</span><span class="ttl">dreamcast_sysasicvar.h: SYSASIC_EVENT_TO_BITMASK(e) is a signed 1 &lt;&lt; 31 for e = 31, 63, 95 -- inside the [0,95] domain SYSASIC_EVENT_RANGE_OK enforces (latent: no defined event has e &amp; 31 == 31)</span><span class="tip">dreamcast_sysasicvar.h: SYSASIC_EVENT_TO_BITMASK(e) is a signed 1 &lt;&lt; 31 for e = 31, 63, 95 -- inside the [0,95] domain SYSASIC_EVENT_RANGE_OK enforces (latent: no defined event has e &amp; 31 == 31) — note: filed 2026-10-09 from the late REVIEW seats on asiceventaddr (Fable 5.1, Opus 5.5; regress/artifacts/asiceventaddr/review_20261009/).  MEASURED: GCC yields 0xffffffff80000000, UBSan reports it (also under build-asan&#x27;s flags); the ledger&#x27;s recorded remedy &#x27;+ SYSASIC_EVENT_RANGE_OK(e)&#x27; is INERT (compiles at 31); the fix is 1u &lt;&lt; ((e) &amp; 31) with the 21 defined events&#x27; masks unchanged.  Witness: detector: (a UBSan compile-and-run row), rung 3 impossible by construction (a guest path needs a new raise site).  Provenance: the kimi substitute and codex on #466&#x27;s pass 2, 2026-08-26.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">armusrwarmap</span><span class="ttl">ARM dyntrans: a USR-mode load or store through a host_load/host_store entry warmed by a PRIVILEGED access to the same page is served without the AP check (AP=0 under the reset S bit: user should get no access)</span><span class="tip">ARM dyntrans: a USR-mode load or store through a host_load/host_store entry warmed by a PRIVILEGED access to the same page is served without the AP check (AP=0 under the reset S bit: user should get no access) — note: filed 2026-10-09 from Fable 5.1&#x27;s armmmuvehicle pass-1 answer (MEASURED, sessions S8 vs S8b, regress/artifacts/armmmuvehicle/pass1_20261009/fable5/): in ONE step N, a privileged LDR of an AP=0 section succeeds and warms the page, MSR CPSR_c,#0x10, the same LDR in USR32 is SERVED (no abort); cold, the USR load takes the permission fault (FSR 0x0d).  cpu_arm_instr_loadstore.c&#x27;s fast path indexes host_load/host_store by virtual page alone and consults is_userpage only for LDRT/STRT; nothing invalidates on a mode change.  Red on HEAD, so not a vehicle row; its own round, armmmuvehicle as the vehicle, S8 as the witness shape.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">armthumbabtlr</span><span class="ttl">cpu_arm.c arm_exception(): Thumb-state aborts save the wrong return address -- data abort LR_abt = instruction + 7, prefetch abort target + 3 (DDI 0100I: + 8 and + 4 in both states)</span><span class="tip">cpu_arm.c arm_exception(): Thumb-state aborts save the wrong return address -- data abort LR_abt = instruction + 7, prefetch abort target + 3 (DDI 0100I: + 8 and + 4 in both states) — note: filed 2026-10-09: retaddr = cpu-&gt;pc (+ 4 for a data abort) + (T ? 2 : 4), and in Thumb state cpu-&gt;pc carries bit 0.  MEASURED by Fable 5.1 on the armmmuvehicle pass-1 sessions S10 (Thumb LDR to an unmapped VA: LR_abt = 0x00008107 for an instruction at 0x8100) and S11 (Thumb BX to 0x100001: LR_abt = 0x00100003); read the same day by grok&#x27;s adversarial job.  DDI 0100I A2.6.6 / A2.6.5 (ddi0100i.txt:2236, :2196) give + 8 and + 4 in both states; IRQ/FIQ are also + 4 in both (:2386, :2440), so the T ? 2 : 4 term is right only for SWI/UND.  A sibling of armthumbabortkill; reachable only with the MMU on, so after armmmuvehicle.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">sgirecontentslice</span><span class="ttl">regress/sgi_re_colourdefault_probe.py: the TLB-array-contents slice of tileptr and three value slices (odd x, y bit 1, mode bit 0) are clause-(e) coverage debt of #519&#x27;s detector -- four readbacks in existing sessions</span><span class="tip">regress/sgi_re_colourdefault_probe.py: the TLB-array-contents slice of tileptr and three value slices (odd x, y bit 1, mode bit 0) are clause-(e) coverage debt of #519&#x27;s detector -- four readbacks in existing sessions — note: filed 2026-10-09 from Fable 5.1&#x27;s 7n-5 ruling (regress/artifacts/fablequeue7n_20261009/fable5_rule7n_35.md, consequence 2), ranked at the top of that file&#x27;s coverage debt and BELOW sgirebufuninit.  The tile-index escapes, the TLB-contents slice and the value slices are ONE species, clause (e): the body tests tile_nr only at &gt;= 256 (tiled) and &gt;= 32 (LIN_A, dev_sgi_re.c -- GPT-6 Astra&#x27;s correction to the ruling&#x27;s &#x27;&lt; 256&#x27;), never for zero, so they are not floor.  Proposed: four readbacks in existing sessions -- a descriptor &gt;= 0x8010 (physical &gt;= 0x100000) at an already-rowed cell (kills the array-contents slice and adds a second anchored address), an odd-x cell, a y with bit 1 set, a mode word with bit 0 set -- one re-table, pin 89 -&gt; 93.  GPT-6 Astra (regress/artifacts/fablequeue7n_20261009/codex_astra_confirm.txt): 89 -&gt; 93 is a PROPOSED budget, not established sufficiency -- the probe&#x27;s own contract says identical-byte writes are invisible and uninitialised-buffer kills need measurement.  Not in-round, not L2, no pass reopened; it ships the next time a measuring seat opens this instrument.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">nullmediumlegs</span><span class="ttl">regress/ppc_rldicl_probe.py (#522) and regress/alpha_tbi_probe.py (#520): floor clause (c) is UNMEASURED and cannot be carried by construction -- neither has runtime gate wiring or an equality pin -- so a measured null-medium leg is owed for each</span><span class="tip">regress/ppc_rldicl_probe.py (#522) and regress/alpha_tbi_probe.py (#520): floor clause (c) is UNMEASURED and cannot be carried by construction -- neither has runtime gate wiring or an equality pin -- so a measured null-medium leg is owed for each — note: [2026-10-18, #565] THE rldicl HALF IS DISCHARGED, MEASURED with the medium this row names: an IDENTITY BODY for X(rldicl) -- decode and retire, write nothing -- built in a scratch clone of build/ scores SCORE 16/24 and reds 11 of gate 13&#x27;s 30 rldicl checks; restored, 24/24, clone cmp-clean and the binary fresh (regress/artifacts/ppcrldiclzero/gatewire_20261018/nullmedium/identity/IDENTITY.out).  Also measured: /bin/true 22 of 30; an absent binary reds the sentinel in the block&#x27;s scoring text and is a SKIP in gate 13 (need_exec).  The probe is now wired with equality pins, so the by-construction reading holds as well.  The alpha_tbi_probe.py half is STILL OWED (its exemption comes due 2026-10-22).  ||  filed 2026-10-09 from Fable 5.1&#x27;s 7n-1 ruling (regress/artifacts/fablequeue7n_20261009/fable5_rule7n_12.md: a by-construction claim is checked by READING the gate&#x27;s pin form, and a table failing that reading owes a measured leg) as corrected by GPT-6 Astra (regress/artifacts/fablequeue7n_20261009/codex_astra_confirm.txt item 1: both probes lack runtime wiring and fixed denominator checks; their exemptions sit in tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py).  The ruling had predicted this population at ZERO.  The leg&#x27;s object, per the carrier&#x27;s clause-(c) block: an instruction handler&#x27;s IDENTITY BODY (decode and retire, write nothing) -- two measured instances at #527.  Their tables&#x27; &#x27;null medium&#x27; labels were whole-file PRE-FIX legs (clause (a)); those labels are corrected in the same commit that filed this row.  ppc_rldicl_probe.py&#x27;s own gate wiring is separately exempt until 2026-10-22 (04f3e7c0).</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">nullmediumsweep</span><span class="ttl">the ~165-unit clause-(c) sweep behind 7n-1&#x27;s &#x27;~16 tables owe a re-run&#x27; has NO durable artifact, and the owner&#x27;s AUDIT-THEN-RE-RUN ruling is recorded only inside an agy report -- the population is unreproducible</span><span class="tip">the ~165-unit clause-(c) sweep behind 7n-1&#x27;s &#x27;~16 tables owe a re-run&#x27; has NO durable artifact, and the owner&#x27;s AUDIT-THEN-RE-RUN ruling is recorded only inside an agy report -- the population is unreproducible — note: filed 2026-10-09 from Fable 5.1&#x27;s 7n-1 answer, &#x27;something ELSE&#x27; item 3 (regress/artifacts/fablequeue7n_20261009/fable5_rule7n_12.md): the list must be PRODUCED from the record before any correction campaign, or the campaign&#x27;s population is a number nobody can check.  7n-1 itself released the campaign (zero closed rounds reopen; a pre-fix leg labelled &#x27;null medium&#x27; is an L4 corrected in place, never a breach) -- so this row owes a reproducible census of the labels, not re-runs.  Low: no decision currently rests on the number.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">fablequeueregress</span><span class="ttl">tools/pipeline/check_fable_queue.py credits ANY regress-phase entry as the flagship&#x27;s regress review, so a row whose only regress entries are another seat&#x27;s reads as reviewed while the owed Fable review is unwritten</span><span class="tip">tools/pipeline/check_fable_queue.py credits ANY regress-phase entry as the flagship&#x27;s regress review, so a row whose only regress entries are another seat&#x27;s reads as reviewed while the owed Fable review is unwritten — note: filed 2026-10-09 from this session&#x27;s queue reconciliation: landiskaux and lcaisalane carry only Opus-seat regress entries and read as discharged; armmsrmodekill did the same until Fable 5.1&#x27;s regress review of #562 landed the same day.  `regress` is FABLE-ONLY by standing directive, so the check should key on seat fable5 (the carrier&#x27;s same-stage, strictly-later marker rule applied to the review itself).  A harness round: the fix owes controls in both directions -- an Opus-only regress entry must be refused, a fable5 one accepted.  ||  [2026-10-09, Fable 5.1&#x27;s regress review of stagetokens, finding 5 (regress/artifacts/fablequeue8n_20261009/regress_harness/fable5_regress_harness.md; fixture regress/artifacts/fablequeue8n_20261009/regress_harness/fx_regresshold/)]: section I&#x27;s regress guarantee is narrower than its docstring.  A CLOSED row whose only regress entry is a live fable5 HELD marker, not named in the queue, passes check_fable_queue.py (rule 3 reads the marker as &#x27;a regress entry&#x27;; rules 1-2 `continue` before the regress phase); check_stage_panels.py ignores regress by design; gen_codex_wall.py lists it and precommit I2 hard-fails a stale wall -- so the hold IS forced into the queue, by I2 rather than I, and check_fable_queue&#x27;s held-and-queued count (2 at HEAD) excludes the 20 regress:fable5 holds the wall carries.  Fix in the same harness round: name I2 as the enforcer in the docstring, or test regress holds before `continue`.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">vmewidthlanes</span><span class="ttl">dev_vme.c: sub-word VME2 accesses -- 40 width/address combinations at 30 offsets inside cased words reach default: (a host kill today), and a cased base accessed at len != 4 is served with word semantics, lane-wrong on big-endian</span><span class="tip">dev_vme.c: sub-word VME2 accesses -- 40 width/address combinations at 30 offsets inside cased words reach default: (a host kill today), and a cased base accessed at len != 4 is served with word semantics, lane-wrong on big-endian — note: filed 2026-10-09 from Fable 5.1&#x27;s 7n-4 ruling (regress/artifacts/fablequeue7n_20261009/fable5_rule7n_4.md, populations 3 and 4) with GPT-6 Astra&#x27;s corrections (regress/artifacts/fablequeue7n_20261009/astra_7n4/codex_astra.txt): 40 width/address combinations at 30 distinct offsets (30 byte accesses + 10 aligned halfword accesses; 16 at the four storing words, 24 at the six other cased words).  &#x27;Serve the containing word&#x27; is REFUTED: big-endian byte lanes +1/+2 come back wrong (+3 and halfword +2 happen to agree), sub-word writes replace the whole backing word, and a T1COUNT read adds 100 and returns the pre-increment value.  Population 4 (Fable&#x27;s ELSE #1): an access AT a cased base with len != 4 -- st.b at 0x88 rewrites the whole VBR word, ld.b there returns the low byte; Astra: a doubleword reaching the callback as ONE length-8 access is not established by the files read.  The in-tree OpenBSD 2.2 guest makes no sub-word VME2 access (every vme2reg field is u_long), so LOW.  The width row takes both populations; the FAULT round for population 1 discloses it and pins the interim behaviour with one channel row (the crimectllane precedent).  Reading only; nothing measured.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">pcc2c040assertxor</span><span class="ttl">dev_pcc2.c&#x27;s C040 arm: `assert = 0;` -&gt; `assert ^= 1;` passes all 18 rows of regress/pcc2_c040_probe.py -- with C040 set and nothing pending it delivers a spurious interrupt on a legal store (clause-(e) debt)</span><span class="tip">dev_pcc2.c&#x27;s C040 arm: `assert = 0;` -&gt; `assert ^= 1;` passes all 18 rows of regress/pcc2_c040_probe.py -- with C040 set and nothing pending it delivers a spurious interrupt on a legal store (clause-(e) debt) — note: filed 2026-10-09 from pcc2c040assertrow&#x27;s review stage: raised by the glm seat of _scratchpad/panel_20261009_191953, MEASURED 18/18 by the main loop (regress/artifacts/pcc2c040kill/assertrow_review_20261009/probe_xor.raw; base 18/18 in probe_base.raw).  GRADED clause (e), not floor, by Fable 5.1&#x27;s final ruling (regress/artifacts/pcc2c040kill/assertrow_review_20261009/fable5_ruling_v3_20261009.md, reversing its own v2) on GPT-6 Astra&#x27;s dissent (regress/artifacts/fablequeue8n_20261009/astra_confirm/codex_astra_n6pcc2.txt): the C040 guarded block&#x27;s only use of `assert` is the WRITE `assert = 0;`, it tests nothing on the entering value, and `if (assert)` sits after the block&#x27;s closing brace, so it cannot dominate the edited line -- under DEPENDS-ON&#x27;s two-item bound and the derived-input rule the cell is not enumerated.  WHAT SURVIVES THE REGRADE: the only guest-visible channel is DELIVERY, which no existing row can vary; the idle state is one byte store in a fresh machine; and the pin is PREDICTED, NOT MEASURED -- a free-running `c040 idle` row (the assert_row() shape with the clmpcc IER store removed, final GENCTL 0x06, breakpoints at vector 0x8 and at completion, want completion; base -&gt; completion, this variant -&gt; 0x8) with a state control (SCCTX readback 0x13: IEN set, INT clear).  OWNER QUESTION, named by the ruling and decided by neither seat: does a repair&#x27;s own write target, tested by the enclosing function&#x27;s next statement, enter DEPENDS-ON? -- ANSWERED THE SAME EVENING by the owner (AskUserQuestion, 2026-10-09): KEEP THE WRITTEN RULE, so this row stays clause-(e) debt.  Ranked below live defects.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">pcc2c040warnedeq</span><span class="ttl">dev_pcc2.c&#x27;s C040 arm: `d-&gt;warned |= (1u &lt;&lt; PCC2_W_C040)` -&gt; `d-&gt;warned = (1u &lt;&lt; PCC2_W_C040)` passes all 18 rows of regress/pcc2_c040_probe.py -- it clears the twelve other width-warning latch bits, so one of those warnings announces again (clause-(e) debt)</span><span class="tip">dev_pcc2.c&#x27;s C040 arm: `d-&gt;warned |= (1u &lt;&lt; PCC2_W_C040)` -&gt; `d-&gt;warned = (1u &lt;&lt; PCC2_W_C040)` passes all 18 rows of regress/pcc2_c040_probe.py -- it clears the twelve other width-warning latch bits, so one of those warnings announces again (clause-(e) debt) — note: filed 2026-10-09 from pcc2c040assertrow&#x27;s review stage: raised by the deepseek and kimi (kimi-k3:cloud) seats of _scratchpad/panel_20261009_191953, MEASURED 18/18 by the main loop (regress/artifacts/pcc2c040kill/assertrow_review_20261009/probe_eq.raw; base 18/18 in probe_base.raw).  Clause (e), not floor (Fable 5.1, regress/artifacts/pcc2c040kill/assertrow_review_20261009/fable5_ruling_v3_20261009.md; GPT-6 Astra concurring): `|=` READS the whole field, but the C040 arm&#x27;s body TESTS only its own bit -- the tested partition, not an absence of reads, is the warrant.  It clears the TWELVE other allocated width bits (the enum holds twelve plus C040), not thirteen; the default-offset warnings use the separate `warned_unimpl` field and are untouched.  `warned` is host-side, so the only guest-visible effect is another latch re-announcing (a floodclass re-arm).  The pin, if worked: extend the `c040 predirty` session with a second ST_H(GENCTL) after the C040 write and count the width-decline announces (want 1, variant 2) -- zero extra sessions.  Disclosed in the probe contract when that probe is next opened.  Ranked below live defects.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">stagetokenscontrols</span><span class="ttl">regress/artifacts/stagetokens/controls_534/run_controls.py: 13 of 49 expectations are reddened by no shipped variant -- twelve measured failable by six one-line extra variants, and the t_reread expectation cannot see filing-vs-grandfathered (a filing-shortcut variant passes 49/49)</span><span class="tip">regress/artifacts/stagetokens/controls_534/run_controls.py: 13 of 49 expectations are reddened by no shipped variant -- twelve measured failable by six one-line extra variants, and the t_reread expectation cannot see filing-vs-grandfathered (a filing-shortcut variant passes 49/49) — note: filed 2026-10-09 from Fable 5.1&#x27;s regress reviews of stagetokens (finding 3) and heldmasked (its one finding) (regress/artifacts/fablequeue8n_20261009/regress_harness/fable5_regress_harness.md; never_reddened.txt; extra_mutants.out).  Coverage debt, not a floor breach: the controls&#x27; contract is variant-centred and all 33 shipped variants are caught.  The thirteen: CSP t_held HOLD, t_annot grandfathered, t_reread one-seat filing, t_nopanel exempt, t_notseat incomplete, t_heldnop HOLD, t_discharged complete; FQ t_notseat short, t_nopanel exempt, t_held queued; DASH annotation / nopanel / notseat renders tok.  Measured with HEAD&#x27;s tools: X_is_held_exact 32/49, X_never_discharge 43/49 (it reds t_discharged, one of the four rows heldmasked&#x27;s closure names), X_notseat_is_answer 45/49, X_annotation_is_answer 45/49, X_nopanel_not_exempt 41/49, X_dash_tok_blank 44/49.  The thirteenth is MISLABELLED: its regex anchors on leading whitespace before t_reread, which every listing line except a VIOLATION replaces with ok/--/.., so it can only assert &#x27;t_reread is not a violation&#x27;; X_filing_is_zero (`if len(got) == 1:` -&gt; `== 0`) passes 49/49.  Shape to adopt, one commit: the seven variants, and re-pin t_reread on its `..    t_reread  review  1/9  filed` line (or rename it).</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="