regress/artifacts/fableheldform\design_20261018\codex_fhfp1.err:908:tools\pipeline\matrix.html:21598:repair 14 FULLY STAGED -- probe edits, contract, PRETABLE, check_pred.py, mutants_r14.py and a map-verified 15-leg driver, all ordered before any run. Three checkers green. NOTHING MEASURED; #530 table 7 still holds the machine, deliberately unraced. Next: fire table 12, then the INTMASK/CONTROL-write swaps Fable requires MEASURED, then the decline carriers</span></span><span class="state st-closed">closed</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-09-25 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] #529 main loop, GXEMUL [087a90]: TABLE 13a (the INTMASK and CONTROL-write label swaps the stop condition required MEASURED): CHECK13A_PASS -- base 204/204, M7_intmasklatch 201/204, M8_ctllatch 201/204, each exact against PRETABLE13a.out.  No INTMASK or CONTROL carrier owed.  PRETABLE written before the table (mtime order); scratch clone /tmp/gxopus_r14 restored cmp-clean, no .MUTANT. || 2026-09-26 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] #529 main loop, GXEMUL [087a90]: TABLE 14 (repair 15: the TIME and REV decline carriers, the entries 13-and-17 pair): CHECK14_PASS, 18 legs exact -- base 218/218 on probe f5e915f6; M3_timelatch and M5_revlatch 214/218 (were 204/204 escapes); M6/M7/M8 215/218; D_nodogclear 216/218.  PRETABLE written before the table (mtime order); scratch clone /tmp/gxopus_r14 restored cmp-clean, no .MUTANT. || 2026-09-26 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] #529 main loop, GXEMUL [087a90]: TABLE 15a (pass 2&#x27;s finding): H_noresetclear and E_noendianclear 218/218, both escapes AS PREDICTED -- the HARD_RESET clear&#x27;s residue had no row; ENDIANESS disclosed.  PRETABLE written before the table (mtime order); scratch clone /tmp/gxopus_r14 restored cmp-clean, no .MUTANT. || 2026-09-26 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] #529 main loop, GXEMUL [087a90]: TABLE 16 (repair 16: the CONTROL arm&#x27;s residue-text count for each clear in both latch states): CHECK16_PASS, 25/25 legs exact on probe 5f770991 (226 rows) -- H_noresetclear and E_noendianclear now detected; W_istlb and W_imklb 226/226 as predicted (disclosed).  PRETABLE written before the table (mtime order); scratch clone /tmp/gxopus_r14 restored cmp-clean, no .MUTANT.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — [EVIDENCE REPAIRED 2026-09-26 by #529: this entry cited `_scratchpad/fable_flagship_20260918.md (brief)`, a volatile brief, while the answer lived only in the transcript -- 87 claude-fable-5-1 turns, 0 refusals, a genuine seat answer.]  **RATIFY** the panel&#x27;s refutation of P2/P3 and the reshaped repair 14; **DISSENT on closure readiness -- two checkable defects sit in the working tree and ONE WOULD RED THE GATE TODAY.**  VERIFIED: `regress/gate_arm.sh`&#x27;s uncommitted hunk pins `crime_width rows run` at **188**, while every repair-14 leg since 09-17 08:34 reads **/204** -- a gate run on this tree reds three checks.  The pin must move to 204 in the same commit as the probe, AFTER the base leg (the `#462` rule).  VERIFIED: there is no `#529` commit at all, and `regress/crime_width_probe.py` is staged `A` but never committed; table 12 was aborted at leg 4 of 15 and re-fired, so the ruling&#x27;s own stop condition -- every enumerated mutant built and killed, the zero carried with its denominator -- is NOT met until that table completes. — evidence: regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/flagship_20260918/fable5_flagship_20260918_answer.txt (the answer, extracted from transcript agent-a2865c082138f4cf6; its brief beside it)</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">R14-PASS1-MEASURED-DESIGN-INVALID</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;R14-PASS1-MEASURED-DESIGN-INVALID&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-17 — CONFIRMED — *** VERDICT: DO NOT SHIP REPAIR 14 AS PROPOSED.  P2 IS FALSE AND P3 IS FALSE, AND IT MEASURED BOTH. SIX MUTANTS, TWO TABLES, PREDICTIONS MATCHED 6 OF 6. *** base 188/188 | PC_imk4r 187/188 reds `gate line&#x27; (POSITIVE CONTROL, reproducing close-8 exactly) | M1_gotolatch 178/188 KILLED on ten rows | **M2_ld278clr 188/188 ESCAPE** | M4_timeplain 184/188 (DISCRIMINATING CONTROL, exactly the four predicted rows) | **M3_timelatch 188/188 TOTAL ESCAPE**. **O1, THE FINDING OF THE ROUND: THE 56-CELL PRODUCT IS THE ACCEPT HALF OF A 112-CELL SPACE.**  It describes only accesses that are SERVICED.  The DECLINE arm -- the thing #529 ADDED -- has its own product {len 1,2} x {R,W} x {7 labels} x {latch}, and the enumeration contains NONE of it.  **Parts A and B are both accept-side, so NEITHER CAN REACH IT.**  This supersedes the deepseek-vs-codex disagreement entirely: they were arguing how to extend the accept-side product while the missing half was a different arm of the same `if&#x27;. **O2: P3 IS FALSE -- THE K-FORM IS LOUD, NOT SILENT.**  It falls into the decline arm, SETS the latch and PRINTS; it escapes because the announce is STOLEN (in `latch x5&#x27;&#x27;s prologue the count stays 1), not because it is absent.  The G-form is the silent one.  **My brief reasoned `it declines silently&#x27; and aimed the repair at value oracles -- reasoning from silence pointed the repair at the wrong channel.** **O3, the Q2 answer, MEASURED: a TWO-LINE edit scores 188/188** -- move `goto crime_declined&#x27; INSIDE the latch block and condition it on `relative_addr != CRIME_TIME&#x27;.  A narrow access at CRIME_TIME that is NOT its session&#x27;s first refusal falls into the switch and advances the guest clock, one of the four defects the fix&#x27;s own comment says the goto prevents.  The SAME edit without the latch conjunct (M4_timeplain) is killed 184/188 on exactly the four predicted rows -- ~2.2 million to one on the raw value -- and the liveness control reads `large&#x27; in BOTH runs, so the channel is live and the difference is the mutant.  **Part A cannot test this at all: a pre-latch session by construction contains no refusal before the cell under test.** **O4: the decline x latch-SET axis derived -- 7 cells, 2 OPEN (REV and TIME)**, on a discriminator that needs no run (does any session refuse at this label more than ONCE?).  *** AND THE PROBE ALREADY KNEW: crime_width_probe.py:1077-1079 states the asymmetry in as many words, derived for a DIFFERENT mutant, and nobody turned it around to ask what it implies for the goto. ***  Two rows in one diff close the axis. **O5: M2_ld278clr is a FIFTH escape and it CONFIRMS my buckets re-derivation independently** -- ACCEPTS entry 46 (ld +0x278) is one of the eight PRE-BLIND entries buckets8.py named, and the only one with neither an equivalence derivation nor a measurement.  The seat reached it by BUILDING A MUTANT; the deriver reached it by READING SESSIONS.  Two roads, same cell. **O6: Part A&#x27;s denominator is 8, not 23** (mirror14.py: N_ENTRIES_WITH_NO_PRELATCH_OBSERVER=8 of 46) -- matching BUCKETS8_rerun.out&#x27;s N_PRE_BLIND=8 exactly, from an independent tool. **O7: Q3 IS UNANSWERABLE AS POSED AND THE PROBE&#x27;S OWN HEADER SAYS SO** -- 2 of the 5 HOST-DIAGNOSTIC and 6 of the 10 EQUIVALENT cells have NO LISTED MEMBERS (crime_width_probe.py:242-257: `a bucket whose members cannot be listed cannot be audited&#x27;).  My brief promoted those counts to a SETTLED PREMISE while its own source flags them unlistable.  **8 of 46 cannot be checked by anyone**, so the nine-entry demand is a FLOOR rather than the answer. O8: four unnamed axes collapse with warrants (cpu-&gt;is_32bit is DEAD CODE on ip32 -- subtype 32 -&gt; R4400 -&gt; isa_level 3 -&gt; is_32bit == 0; ncpus; use_fb; physical_ram_in_mb).  **A DOMAIN DEPENDENCY NOBODY HAD STATED:** a real MIPS guest emits len in {1,2,4,8} exactly, but memory_rw.c:495-523 CLAMPS len at a device&#x27;s end and can emit 1..7 -- inert here ONLY because DEV_CRIME_LENGTH is 0x280, a multiple of 8.  That makes codex&#x27;s reachability argument conditional on a constant rather than absolute.  Also: an accepted HARD_RESET write TERMINATES its session, so Part B costs one NEW SESSION per cell; and #529&#x27;s own diff created a stale citation -- OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md:5574 cites dev_sgi_ip32.c:698, now :728. O9, ITS OWN ERRORS RECORDED BY THE SEAT RATHER THAN BY ME: a row-to-session off-by-one in its deriver (found pre-ship; buckets8.py unaffected), the backslash trap twice, and **a CRLF script that EXITED 0 HAVING BUILT AND RUN NOTHING** -- caught only because two seconds is impossible for two 17-minute probes.  No damage: the cd failed before the sentinel was dropped. FOOTPRINT CLEAN: no project tree written, all four fork copies still md5 8c1d1545..., clone sentinel cleared, source cmp-clean, binary -nt source, restored byte-identical to base. — evidence: regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/repair14_20260916/opus_pass1.md (30 KB) and opus_pass1_work/ -- PREDICT.md 23:58:36 and PREDICT2.md 00:04:17 against builds at 00:00:0x / 00:18:4x; six probe logs all ending CRIMEP_DONE; mirror14.py, mutants14.py, frozen drivers kill14.run-000006.sh / kill14b.run-001836.sh</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">R14-PASS1-REFIRE-ANSWERED</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;R14-PASS1-REFIRE-ANSWERED&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-17 — MANUAL — *** THE RE-FIRE WORKED: 353 KB streamed, ZERO content-filter flags, 7,826 b of verdict.  SAME SEAT, SAME QUESTIONS, SAME TREE -- only neutral vocabulary, reading scoped to src/ + regress/*.py, and the edit-construction question dropped.  The section-C5 remedy is validated a second time, on the seat it was minted from. ***  VERDICT: repair 14 needs a revised coverage model.  **ITS DEEPEST FINDING REFRAMES THE DOMAIN AND CUTS AGAINST THE OTHER SEATS&#x27; REMEDY**: adding lane and PROM-window state mechanically gives 224 nominal tuples, but that MISREPRESENTS REACHABILITY -- the MIPS producer checks natural alignment and the CRIME switch matches the EXACT offset, so every named label has the lane bit CLEAR and a 4-byte access to a register&#x27;s low lane reaches `default&#x27;.  The lane is NOT a free factor, so the corrected enumeration is REACHABILITY-CONSTRAINED rather than a cross-product -- meaning deepseek&#x27;s remedy (state the six-factor product) would have been wrong in the opposite direction.  Two seats pushed the enumeration opposite ways and the truth is neither.  **A RECORDS FINDING NO OTHER SEAT REACHED:** the shipped probe has NO direct value assertion for accepted CONTROL `lw +0x08&#x27; -- it runs through ACCEPTS where its destination is overwritten, `devsig hi&#x27; checks REV and `acc ctl ld&#x27; checks EIGHT-byte CONTROL -- so the equivalence derivation is sound but its claimed supporting row is missing.  That independently confirms the close-8 reading that table 11&#x27;s C_ctl4r leg was vacuous for want of an ORACLE rather than an ACCESS.  Also named four arms whose effects the common tail does NOT reproduce (DOG&#x27;s register effects, INTSTAT&#x27;s interrupt-LINE update, TIME&#x27;s update, REV&#x27;s PC effect), and independently enumerated the instrument at 51 sessions / 188 uniquely named rows -- a free cross-check on the denominator every score in this campaign is quoted against. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260916_234606/</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">R14-PASS1</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;R14-PASS1&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-16 — MANUAL — GO-WITH-CHANGES.  **FOUND F3, AND IT REFUTES A CLAIM OF MINE USING THE PROBE&#x27;S OWN HEADER.**  My brief said an early `return&#x27; in place of `goto crime_declined&#x27; would skip the interrupt recomputation and memory_writemax64, &#x27;a defect the shipped code does not have&#x27;.  crime_width_probe.py:269-272 says the opposite and gives the warrant: the two are EQUIVALENT on every channel because memory_rw pre-zeroes a device read buffer (#95) and nothing on a declined access writes HARDINT or SOFTINT, so the tail&#x27;s restore and recompute are identities -- measured 40/40 in kill table 1 and formally DISCLOSED.  UPHELD: the statements are mechanically skipped and the skipping is UNOBSERVABLE, so the consequence I attached is what is false.  I imported a correct general caution (the four-readers common-tail lesson) into the one site where it had been measured not to apply. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260916_234606/</span></span></td><td class="c legacy"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">R14-PASS1</span><span class="tip">legacy -- verdict unclassified: d = &#x27;R14-PASS1&#x27; is outside ✓ ✕ ⏸ …; read the note for the outcome — 2026-09-17 — MANUAL — NOT RATIFIED as written -- and the strongest answer of the panel.  It reached the 46-vs-56 finding INDEPENDENTLY and supplied the MECHANISM no other seat did: 23 is a count of ACCEPTS ENTRIES rowed post-latch by repair 13, not of product cells, and MANY ENTRIES MAP TO ONE CELL (the CONTROL writes 0x0201 / 0x0001 / 0 / 0x0200 / 0x0100 are five entries of ONE cell), which is why no re-count could ever reconcile 46 with 56.  **IT THEN DERIVED WHY INTSTAT 4R ESCAPES EVERYTHING**: using 23 as the class-closure denominator is how IST 4R falls through -- it is not in the 23 because the SET side is already pinned by `istat ctl&#x27;, and it is still open on CLEAR.  **THE MISSING FLOOR CELL, NAMED WITH ITS ORACLE REQUIREMENT: INTSTAT 4R, latch-CLEAR, with SOFTINT|HARDINT SEEDED NONZERO** -- sharper than my own criterion, which said `driven pre-refusal with an oracle&#x27; and did not say what the oracle must contain.  ADDS A DESIGN CONSTRAINT I had not stated: G_clr_imk4r 187/188 reddening `gate line&#x27; must STAY the positive control in the 188-row instrument, so the next closing pass keeps a CLEAR-half control that is not TIME -- repair 14 owes a check that it does not disturb it.  ALSO: P1 was NOT the full enclosing function; the omitted prelude at 229-235 (CONTROL = ENDIANESS 0x100 on every access) IS the warrant for the CONTROL-4R equivalence the packet asserted without it.  A section-D violation of mine. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260916_234606/</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — CONFIRMED — **VERDICT: DO NOT RATIFY AS WRITTEN.**  *** AN UNREAD REVIEW ON AN IN-FLIGHT ROUND, RECORDED 2026-09-17 -- it answered on 2026-09-16 and had no cell until section G surfaced it. ***  Transport: `kimi-k3:cloud` SUBSTITUTE, so PACKET-FED; its claims are the packet&#x27;s, walked rather than re-derived from the tree. **IT WALKED THE ARITHMETIC RATHER THAN REASONING ABOUT IT, which is what the brief asked for and what makes its finding checkable:** `2x2x2x7 = 56` (seven case labels, six named plus `default`); `23 + 8 + 10 + 5 = 46`; *** therefore **56 - 46 = 10 CELLS APPEAR IN NO CATEGORY** ***.  It names the settling fact rather than guessing at the cause -- *the per-cell disposition table* -- and says plainly that the ACCEPTS-to-cell map is not settleable from the packet. **FINDING 1 -- THE PACKET CONTRADICTS ITSELF:** P4 claims *&quot;the latch-CLEAR state is driven by session 40 (`latch x5`) 