d, not #392: the floor is the diff-closed 56-cell product.  **Q1, the units: the FLOOR is the 23 open guest-visible cells (31 minus the 8 already pinned), NOT all 28 latch-SET mutants and NOT all 56 product cells** -- a mutant at an equivalent or pinned cell teaches nothing, a row at a cell no mutant reaches is unfalsifiable, so the floor is the INTERSECTION.  PRETABLE 11 carries the WHOLE product with per-cell disposition: 23 rowed, 8 already-pinned, 10 equivalent (no row), 5 host-diagnostic (clause-(e), disclosed with F1/F1b/F3&#x27;s measurements); 10+5+8+23 = 46.  Q3: table 11 AND closing pass 8, BOTH -- retyped rows are measured not assumed, and pass 8 VERIFIES the enumeration cell-by-cell and must close on a zero carried WITH its denominator.  D1&#x27;s grade was under-determined while D7 was punted and is now SECURED by it.  D3/D4 (the two disclosures I flagged) UPHELD, each verified against the seat&#x27;s measurements and each with an independent second reason.  L4 it names: its own RA3, and the header&#x27;s `46 kinds&#x27; vs `46 ENTRIES, not 46 kinds&#x27; inconsistency (grok&#x27;s nit, confirmed) -- both corrected in place. — record: 2026-09-17 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] *** WRONG RECORD, corrected 2026-09-26: MEASURED from the subagent transcript (per-message `model&#x27; and `stop_reason&#x27;; _scratchpad/agent_models.py), the answer this entry credits to fable5 was WRITTEN BY claude-opus-4-8 at 06:25:19Z (agent a2bba4bc2896433b4) -- claude-fable-5-1 ended a turn with stop_reason &quot;refusal&quot; at 2026-09-17T06:17:21Z and the Agent tool re-ran the rest on opus-4-8, keeping the seat&#x27;s identity line.  Kept as an opus-4-8 READING, not a fable5 answer; the file carries a dated provenance note since 2026-09-26; the first-hand ruling is regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/rerule_20260925/fable5_rerule_529_20260925.md (the first-hand fable5 ruling of 2026-09-25, entered below; it re-anchors C3, D7, Q3 and STOP). ***  *** RULING: REPAIR 14 IS TWO EARNED CLASS-CLOSURES PLUS ONE FLOOR CELL -- NOT NINE CARRIERS AND NOT AN OPEN-ENDED HUNT.  SHIP IN ONE DIFF. *** **THE ONE SUBSTANTIVE OVERTURN NO SEAT REACHED, AND IT IS THE BEST THING IN THE ROUND: THE DECLINE FACE IS UNDER-MEASURED.**  `latch_label()&#x27; has run at exactly THREE of its five guest-observable labels -- INTSTAT (killed), TIME (escape), REV (escape) -- while **INTMASK and CONTROL-WRITE are DERIVED COVERED AND NEVER MEASURED**.  Fable&#x27;s own words: *building the two measured escapes and deriving the rest is the exact move (`derive instead of measure&#x27;) that M5_revlatch was built to punish.*  O4 DERIVED REV open and M5 MEASURED it open; deriving INTMASK/CONTROL-write COVERED is the same gamble in the other direction.  **Closure is not claimable until both swaps are built and scored by the M6 method.** Q1: adopts the Opus spine.  ACCEPT SIDE -- entry 21 in BOTH latch states, seeded above bit 31 (verified: +0x10 &amp; 4 == 0 takes the high lane at :294, so without the seed the row is `devsig hi&#x27; again, and POST is genuinely blind too since entry 21&#x27;s POST drivers [19, 26] are BOTH oracle-less); entries 32/33 via the clock-advance GAPPED channel; entry 46.  CUT AS EQUIVALENT with derivations into the contract: 1, 3 (REV is read nowhere -- Fable grepped: 5 hits, no consumer, prelude re-forces it), 4, 8 (4R high lane answers 0, and so does a decline).  Entry 40 -&gt; HOST-DIAGNOSTIC.  **It upholds that `nine&#x27; counted ENTRIES and spent them as ROWS.** **ENTRY 14 IS GRADED L2, NOT DEBT** -- `p acc ctl msg&#x27; counts the `sw&#x27; twin and not the `sd&#x27;: same address, same body-tested value, other width, no row.  *The #499 cell reproduced INSIDE the row that closed the #499 family.*  Entries 13/17 neither flat-included nor flat-filed: run the CHANNEL check, L2 if a body-tested-partition mutant escapes, clause (e) if the count cannot vary. A11 FOLDED INTO A12: the CONTROL 4R row is the ctl4r+ctl0c PAIR, never `lw +0x08&#x27; alone (vacuous, 0==0). Q2: ONE DIFF STANDS AND IT IS NOT #392.  The #392 test is *does each pass find a NEW class?* -- this chain does not: exactly TWO classes, each at TWO measured instances, both enumerations diff-closed.  STOP CONDITION in three parts: every enumerated mutant built and killed; the zero carried WITH ITS DENOMINATOR; the contract naming covered vs deliberately-not.  Terminates on the first clean sweep. Q3: THE NEW FLOOR CLAUSE IS **ADOPTED WITH THREE AMENDMENTS** -- (1) make it a THIRD DISJUNCT of the 2026-09-09 label clause rather than a standalone, because the carrier forbids two statements of one rule; (2) restrict to GUEST-OBSERVABLE SIDE EFFECT rather than `non-null body&#x27;, since the Opus wording would owe a row for default&#x27;s host-only debug(); (3) discharge is the label-swap mutant, folding the new axis into the existing measured-kill and CHANNEL machinery so nothing is new but the enumeration SOURCE.  Bounded to the labels of the ONE skipped dispatch in the enclosing function.  **And it carries its own expiry: minted from one device, so its first reuse elsewhere should CHECK the enumeration, not merely obey it** -- the freshly-minted-exemplar rule applied by the seat to its own ruling. Q4: upholds every reversal the panel forced (O1/112 withdrawn, O2&#x27;s redirect withdrawn, A11 vacuous, A13 self-applied to 1-of-2); keeps D1 OPEN as a CONDITION rather than a number; and **reverses NOTHING in the fix direction -- the goto de-fatalisation itself is unchallenged across two passes, and the entire dispute is detector coverage.** ORDER: (1) entry 14, sharpest and cheapest L2; (2) decline closure = TIME + REV carriers PLUS the INTMASK/CONTROL-write swap VERIFICATION; (3) accept closure = 21x2 seeded, 32/33, 46; (4) A11-&gt;A12 pair; (5) 13/17 after the CHANNEL check; (6) FILE A9&#x27;s kills, D1&#x27;s split-width routing, and the +2 translation. — record: 2026-09-17 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] *** WRONG RECORD, corrected 2026-09-26: this verification res