the recorder&#x27;s words, not the seat&#x27;s -- the file is the record; the second records audit found this labelled an excerpt): it largely upholds the dispositions but would overturn F2 FIRST, on the ENDIANESS scope objection  Dispositions: CHANGELOG #529 and regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/repair16_f2_20260926/ (the F2 packet and the flagship ruling). — evidence: regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/repair16_f2_20260926/panels/panel_20260926_053828/ollama_minimax.txt</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-26 — THE CHAIN CLOSES — #529 FINAL, the FLAGSHIP seat (regress is fable5-only): the enumeration closed on repair 16&#x27;s F2 pass with its denominator (the ruling&#x27;s Q2), CONDITIONAL on the text corrections (r17, r18, r19, r20, r21, then r22 -- the committed text), a base leg on the final bytes (final529r22_20261002/probe_base_r22.raw: Base leg on r22 against table 16&#x27;s base binary (2026-10-02, WALL 1235 s): 226/226, CONTROL OK; 21 differing row pairs against table 16&#x27;s base log -- 15 timing-dependent TIME values and the 6 rows of the three rewritten notes -- and 0 row pair(s) differing only in column padding after normalising those; no want, got or verdict column differs (`final529r22_20261002/probe_base_r22.raw`).; r21&#x27;s leg, final529r21_20260930/probe_base_r21.raw: Base leg on r21 against table 16&#x27;s base binary (2026-10-01, WALL 1233 s): 226/226, CONTROL OK; 23 differing row pairs against table 16&#x27;s base log -- 17 timing-dependent TIME values and the 6 rows of the three rewritten notes -- and 0 row pair(s) differing only in column padding after normalising those; no want, got or verdict column differs (`final529r21_20260930/probe_base_r21.raw`).; r20&#x27;s leg, final529r20_20260930/: Base leg on r20 against table 16&#x27;s base binary (2026-09-30, WALL 1229 s): 226/226, CONTROL OK; 27 differing row pairs against table 16&#x27;s base log -- 21 timing-dependent TIME values and the 6 rows of the three rewritten notes -- and 4 row pair(s) differing only in column padding after normalising those; no want, got or verdict column differs (`final529r20_20260930/probe_base_r20.raw`).; the r18 and r19 legs, final529r18_20260926/ and final529r19_20260930/, 226/226 each), the S_rst4clr attribution kept durable (opus_f2/), GPT-6 Astra&#x27;s confirmation and #549-first ordering; no row was ordered.  The final probe is code-identical to repair 16 but for three row notes (final529r17_20260926/mk_r17.py.txt, final529r18_20260926/mk_r18.py.txt, final529r19_20260930/mk_r19.py.txt, final529r20_20260930/mk_r20.py.txt, final529r21_20260930/mk_r21.py.txt, final529r22_20261002/mk_r22.py.txt). — evidence: regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/repair16_f2_20260926/fable5_f2_adjudication.md</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — CONFIRMED — *** #529&#x27;s L1 IS CLOSED: the ctl0c pair is DISCHARGED BY A MEASURED KILL.  The rows stay. ***  base 204/204, M_ctl0c_decline 202/204, with acc ctl0c AND p acc ctl0c FAILING and both ctl4r rows UNMOVED -- an exact match to the prediction written into the mutator BEFORE the run.  Controls: probe frozen cmp-clean, clone cmp-clean against SEC at start, **binary DIFFERS from base so the edit was live in the object**, clone restored cmp-clean with binary-nt-source.  *** THE REAL FINDING: THE ROWS WERE NEVER VACUOUS -- THE MUTANT SET WAS INCOMPLETE. ***  `acc ctl0c&#x27; wants 0x100, and that value comes from the WIDTH ARM, which runs BEFORE the register switch; +0x0c has no case label and lands in `default:&#x27;, a debug print only.  So a decline at `default:&#x27; cannot move it, and G_clr_ctl4r&#x27;s `relative_addr == CRIME_CONTROL&#x27; (0x08) never touches 0x0c.  All fifteen legs were aimed where this row&#x27;s value does not come from.  The discharging mutant declines BEFORE the width arm (`if (relative_addr == 0x0c) goto crime_declined;&#x27;) -- clause (d): keep the guard, reroute its effect.  *A row whose value is produced before the switch cannot be moved by any mutant that edits the switch, however many you build.* — evidence: regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/ctl0c_discharge_20260917/ (RUN.out sentinel KILLCTL0C_DONE, VERDICT.md, mutants_ctl0c.py, logs/probe_base.raw 204/204, logs/probe_M_ctl0c_decline.raw 202/204)</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-closed"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">fbctrlportkill</span><span class="ttl">dev_fbctrl.c: the PORT arm ACCEPTS an out-of-range port number with a warning and STORES it, and the DATA arm then calls exit(1) on that same stored value -- a two-step, guest-driven host kill where the first step looks handled</span><sup class="b b-A">A</sup><span class="tip">dev_fbctrl.c: the PORT arm ACCEPTS an out-of-range port number with a warning and STORES it, and the DATA arm then calls exit(1) on that same stored value -- a two-step, guest-driven host kill where the first step looks handled — commits: 8ea26abb — #549 CLOSES.  dev_fbctrl.c&#x27;s PORT arm refuses any selector &gt;= 8 compared on the full 64-bit value, keeps the previous one and announces once per device; the DATA arm&#x27;s check stays as a tripwire.  The detector (fbctrl_port_probe.py, 117 rows, 16 sessions) went through eight panels and six variant tables (the last: 297 edits, 267 red, 30 disclosed, zero prediction mismatches); the verifying pass&#x27;s floor breach was repaired in-round (v6, session B), and v6&#x27;s adjudication closed the chain with wording (v6b, then v6c with GPT-6 Astra&#x27;s corrections, comment-only).  codex walled on the five 2026-09-25 panels (re-fired and Astra&#x27;s confirmation after the 07:01 reset).  Filed: fbctrlcmdkill, fbctrloffkill, fbctrltwoinst, scoreclaimsrawdoc, fbctrlportdebt.  Badge A: the main loop adjudicated its own round&#x27;s records. — witness: probe:regress/artifacts/fbctrlportkill_20260924/witness_HEAD/fbctrl_port_witness.py.txt -- on HEAD f4f601c4&#x27;s unmodified -E testmips, arm K (PORT=9 refused-then-stored, then a DATA read) ends the process exit=1 while arm L&#x27;s LIVENESS and DEVICE-SIGNATURE controls are green (witness_HEAD.out); the detector regress/fbctrl_port_probe.py is 117/117 on the fix and red on HEAD&#x27;s arm (M_revert 54/117, table6/TABLE.out)</span></span><span class="state st-closed">closed</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-24 — PROCEED WITH CHANGES — #549 PASS 1, the FLAGSHIP seat&#x27;s RE-ISSUE, fired LAST (agent a79342bd...; claude-fable-5-1, 16:12:11Z).  Verdict, verbatim: PROCEED WITH CHANGES. — evidence: regress/artifacts/fbctrlportkill_20260924/fable5_p1b.md — record: 2026-09-24 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] The flagship seat&#x27;s FIRST pass-1 answer: written by claude-opus-4-8 (16:07:35Z) a