H != 0 [CORRECTED 2026-10-18 at the #527 closure (GPT-6 Astra): the bit counts are wrong -- for a non-wrapping mask the defect overwrote the LOW SH bits that must survive, and for a wrapping mask it omitted the required insertion into positions 0..63-SH (OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md, `ppcrldimimask` DESIGNED 2026-09-10).] — commits: 7e39a49 22c278cd — CLOSED by its closure-records commit (2026-10-18): #527 (7e39a49e, 2026-09-12) stopped X(rldimi)&#x27;s rotate loop from consuming its own shift count -- the post-decrement had left sh == -1, so every insert mask was built to bit 63 -- and made the mask walk circular.  Detector: regress/ppc_rldimi_probe.py, 29 rows, wired into gate 13 (gate_ppc.sh, pin 29; PASS 110 checks at the time, regress/artifacts/ppcrlwimiwidth/gate_ppc_20260912.log).  Kill table 3 (regress/artifacts/ppcrlwimiwidth/killtable3_20260912/SCORES.txt): the fix 29/29, the pre-fix HEAD leg 17/29, the identity body 13/29, all nine D_ mutants killed (the joint table: 17 legs, zero escapes).  The repair chain CLOSED on the §F2 adjudication pass by Fable 5.1&#x27;s ruling (regress/artifacts/xscaleinten/fable_adjudication_20260912.md: zero floor breaches, denominator named).  This row CARRIED #527&#x27;s five residuals by the 2026-10-02 disposition (regress/artifacts/idlessaudit_20261002/AGY_FLAGS_DISPOSITION.md: &#x27;the carrier owes its recorded work whenever its round runs&#x27;); they move to `ppc527residual` (LOW) in this commit, so no named work closes with the row. — witness: probe:regress/artifacts/ppcrldimimask/opus_ppc_rldimi_witness_20260911.py — note: [2026-10-18, CLOSED] The closure-records commit closed the row on Fable 5.1&#x27;s 2026-09-12 ruling; REGRESS is held for the flagship (hold_question).</span></span><span class="state st-closed">closed</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-closed"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td